# genproductions-style proc card — cards/<process_name>/<process_name>_proc_card.dat
#
# Unlike an interactive `.mg5` session (see the mg5 skill's mg5_card_template.mg5),
# this file has no `launch` — gridpack_generation.sh drives generation,
# integration-grid setup, and the test run itself. Keep it to import/generate/output.

# Only needed for loop-induced / NLO processes; harmless otherwise.
# set low_mem_multicore_nlo_generation True

# --- Model import -----------------------------------------------------------
# Pick ONE of the three cases below (pitfall 1 in SKILL.md).
#
# (a) Stock model MG5 already ships — bare name:
#   import model loop_sm-ckm_no_b_mass
#
# (b) BSM model published to the CMS generators web area — bare name, matching
#     the directory name INSIDE the archive. Also create a sibling file
#     cards/<process_name>/<process_name>_extramodels.dat containing just the
#     archive filename, e.g.  my_bsm_model.tgz
#     genproductions wgets it from cms-project-generators and unpacks it into
#     the sandboxed MG5's models/ before generation.
#   import model my_bsm_model
#
# (c) Private UFO still on local disk — absolute path, NO _extramodels.dat.
#     MG5 resolves this during code generation, which runs on the machine
#     invoking gridpack_generation.sh. Fine for private studies; breaks if
#     generation is farmed to batch nodes without a shared filesystem.
import model /absolute/path/to/<UFO_MODEL_DIR_NAME>
#
# In all three cases the finished gridpack is self-contained: the tarball
# packs mgbasedir (including models/) and process, so CMSSW needs no copy
# of the UFO at showering time.

# --- Process ------------------------------------------------------------
# Replace with your validated process (validate interactively first — mg5 skill).
# For a BSM process, decide here whether decays are computed in MG5
# (comma/parenthesis chains, or an explicit n-body ME with NP=N — see the mg5
# skill) or left to Pythia/BuildDecayTableTool downstream.
generate p p > <your process>
# add process p p > <your process> j   # optional: +1 jet, needs MLM matching
#                                        # downstream (see pitfalls.md)

output <process_name> -nojpeg
